		{
			dependencies: ["73F7C99EE4ABCE4F"]
			description: [
				"&eDiamond is crystalline carbon. Its extreme hardness comes from a three-dimensional network of strong bonds, although a hard diamond can still chip along cleavage planes.&r"
				""
				"&eOverworld diamond deposits occur from Y -63 to 0, favoring the middle of that range. They are much scarcer than iron or copper.&r"
			]
