		{
			dependencies: ["73F7C99EE4ABCE4F"]
			description: [
				"&eSulfur is a yellow nonmetal. In natural geology it can occur around volcanic vents or in deposits associated with sulfur-bearing minerals.&r"
				""
				"&eSmall Overworld sulfur deposits span Y -63 to 63. Their native sulfur powder supplies gunpowder and sulfur chemistry. The sulfur dust separated from galena, sphalerite, pentlandite and chalcocite is a distinct stock.&r"
			]
			disable_toast: true
