		{
			dependencies: ["73F7C99EE4ABCE4F"]
			description: [
				"&eSmall tin deposits occur at Y -63 to 160. The raw material supplies tin through powder smelting; cassiterite is the larger mineral-band source.&r"
				""
				"&eTin combines with copper to make bronze. In real metallurgy, its low melting point and resistance to corrosion also make it useful in solder and protective coatings.&r"
			]
			disable_toast: true
