		{
			dependencies: ["450EC9FCCFB49FA9"]
			description: [
				"&eLignite is a low-rank coal, generally browner, softer and more moisture-rich than bituminous coal. It represents an intermediate stage in the transformation of buried plant matter.&r"
				""
				"&eOrdinary lignite bands begin at Y 0-70. Sandy Caves contain more frequent deposits from Y -20 to 63. It is a carbon feedstock, including for the Carbofusor culture's conversion to bituminous coal.&r"
